                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="177" value="1. Now here in hte virtual directory pnpm install/download all hte versions of that same package&lt;div&gt;2. and then in the cache fodler pnpm hardlink this to folder, and then this hardlink one is symlinked to the another folder name &quot;pkg&quot;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. now if the cache hash folder is deleted from the cache dir, now if run the prune cmd, it will now also delete that package version from this dlx virtual folder for that specific package&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="2010" y="290" width="680" height="120" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="178" value="&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;why not directly execute from the virtual dir:&amp;nbsp; - then how pnpm come to that this is a temporary packge, if it does maintain the cache dir for that package&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;pnpm has one habit, that will always use the symlink files, but that symlinked package wont be directly hard linked to its stores, instead pnpm will create a sperate folder that will be hardlink to the files in hte store and then this hardlink dir will be used to symlink&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;install multiple dlx pacakge , install different versions of same packages then notice the virturl dir,&amp;nbsp; and then delete one hte hash folder from the cache, then run prune cmd and again inspect the virtual dir for that specific package folder&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="2810" y="250" width="480" height="210" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
